  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: RenewableTechNigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the consortium is to support the Nigerian renewable energy sector to meet the rising energy demand by providing clean renewable energy, while simultaneously supporting Dutch companies with their market entrance and expansion into the Nigerian market.The goal of the consortium is to facilitate the energy transition in Nigeria and contribute to combatting climate change (SDG 13), with the objectives accomplished through:&#x2022;	Developing affordable and accessible renewable energy solutions through the integration of Dutch design, knowledge, technology and equipment into renewable energy solutions suited to the Nigerian context;&#x2022;	Developing a platform for improved knowledge transfer, capacity building and increased trade and investment between Dutch and Nigerian companies.&#x2022;	Strengthen collaboration between Dutch and Nigerian companies in the renewable energy sector.&#x2022;	Being the flagship project under the new BHOS policy (2022-2025), with the ability to expand beyond the initial project scope.The impact cluster partners will contribute to providing affordable and clean energy (SDG 7) by demonstrating the use of solar hybrid solutions, providing an alternative to expensive and polluting diesel generators. At the same time, the cluster partners will actively explore opportunities to expand the existing technical workforce in the renewable energy sector, providing decent work to young Nigerians and facilitating economic growth (SDG 8), tackling financing issues and policy development to foster the Nigerian business climate (SDG 8). By joining forces, this consortium will drive long-term impact and act to enable cross-sector initiatives to contribute directly to the global energy transition in Nigeria (SDG 17).</narrative>
  </description>
